From: Claude <claude@local>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 08:29:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Notifications: mark-all-as-read button + auto-clear on errand
 status view

Chat already cleared its own notifications on open (ChatThread had an
inline fire-and-forget update) -- confirmed by reading the file
closely, that half of the report was already working. The other half
wasn't: neither errand detail screen ((user) Track Errand or (scout)
Errand Detail) ever marked status-change notifications
(errand_accepted, errand_delivered, errand_confirmed, balance_request_*,
proof_submitted, etc.) as read, even when the person was actively
looking at that exact status on screen.

- lib/notificationsReadState.ts: markErrandNotificationsRead(errandId)
  and markAllNotificationsRead(), shared by every call site instead of
  each screen reimplementing the same update() call
- ChatThread.tsx: now calls the shared helper instead of its own
  inline duplicate
- Both errand detail screens: call markErrandNotificationsRead on
  every loadData() run, which useFocusEffect already re-triggers on
  every visit, not just first mount -- so revisiting an errand you'd
  already seen the status of clears it every time, not only once
- NotificationsList.tsx: 'Mark all read' button in the header, disabled
  (dimmed) when there's nothing unread to clear

Verified with tsc --noEmit -- the three warnings that showed up in
ChatThread.tsx are pre-existing implicit-any lines untouched by this
7-line diff, confirmed by diffing against HEAD.
